#====================================================================
# E264 — Metadata-derived signed ELF adapter for legacy *-config probes
#====================================================================

id:                     E264
trigger_tool:           configure|conan|autotools
phase:                  configuration
error_signature:        configure: error: .*config.*not found|Permission denied.*-config|cannot execute.*-config|could not run.*-config

severity:               2
category:               dependency-discovery|autotools|conan|hmdfs|elf-signing
match_keywords:         configure, *-config, geos-config, Conan metadata, cpp_info, HMDFS, signed ELF, dependency discovery, legacy helper
title:                  Bridge legacy *-config probes with a metadata-derived signed ELF adapter

root_cause:             A legacy configure script may require an executable *-config helper even when the Conan dependency exposes only structured CMake or pkg-config metadata. A shell shim in the package cache is not a reliable executable contract on HMDFS, while hard-coded include and library paths bind the recipe to one cache layout.
affected_scope:         Conan recipes for Autotools or custom configure consumers that must execute a legacy dependency-query helper although the packaged dependency exposes equivalent include, library, version, and link metadata through Conan.
verification_cmd:       Compare every supported helper query with the resolved Conan dependency metadata; reject missing metadata and unknown arguments; verify a target ELF with a valid signature; then run configure and a real consumer against the same exact dependency graph.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           metadata-derived-native-config-adapter
rec_description:        Generate a minimal C helper in the build folder from the resolved dependency cpp_info values, compile it with the active Conan C compiler, sign the resulting target ELF when the executor requires signed binaries, and pass its absolute path through the upstream --with-<name>config option. Implement only the query surface actually consumed by upstream and fail closed for unsupported arguments or absent metadata.
rec_command:            |
  dep = self.dependencies["<name>"].cpp_info
  # Fail if required include or library metadata is absent.
  # Escape values as C string literals, generate one small query program,
  # compile it with tools.build:compiler_executables, sign the final ELF,
  # and pass --with-<name>config=<absolute helper path> to configure.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-generated-c-helper

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      verified-provider-native-helper
fallback_description:   Use a provider-supplied native *-config executable only when it belongs to the exact resolved package revision and its outputs are verified against Conan metadata.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       (storage/Users|\.conan2).*(-I|-L|includedir|libdir)|hard.?cod.*(include|lib).*-config
forbid_1_reason:        Hard-coded cache or device paths do not follow the resolved package revision and break in fresh Conan homes.
forbid_1_consequence:   Configure may bind to stale headers or libraries, or fail when the cache layout changes.
forbid_2_pattern:       write.*(\.sh|shell).*config|echo.*(-I|-L).*>.*-config
forbid_2_reason:        A generated shell shim still depends on direct script execution from a filesystem that may reject it.
forbid_2_consequence:   Dependency discovery remains blocked before compilation even though all metadata is present.
forbid_3_pattern:       unknown.*return 0|argc.*return 0|default.*success.*-config
forbid_3_reason:        Treating unknown queries as success silently weakens the upstream helper contract.
forbid_3_consequence:   Configure can accept incomplete flags and fail later with mismatched headers, unresolved symbols, or a wrong ABI.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E077]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               doc/E264.md
last_updated:           2026-08-08
source_event:           librttopo 1.1.0.1 and libspatialite 5.1.0.1 generated geos-config ELF adapters from the exact geos/3.13.1 Conan metadata

authors:                2301_80739235 <2047361658@qq.com>
